# __DISPLAY_NAME__

A platform micro-frontend (`mfeId: __MFE_ID__`, React __REACT_MAJOR__{{#tecton}}, Tecton{{/tecton}}) scaffolded with
`platform create`. It is built with Vite and TanStack Router, mounted by the shell under
`__ROUTE_PREFIX__` in its own React root, and described by a generated manifest.

## Commands

| Command          | What it does                                                                     |
| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `pnpm dev`       | Vite dev server; dev manifest at `http://localhost:5173/platform-manifest.json` |
| `pnpm build`     | Production build (`dist/`), manifest generation and validation                  |
| `pnpm manifest`  | Print the generated manifest                                                    |
| `pnpm validate`  | Structure, identity, configuration, generated files and manifest checks         |
| `pnpm lint`      | ESLint with the platform shareable config (`@platform/cli/eslint`)              |
| `pnpm test`      | Vitest unit tests (`src/**/*.test.tsx`)                                         |
| `pnpm typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit`                                                                  |

## Layout

```
mfe.config.ts            manifest-affecting options (displayName, navigation, env…)
src/mfe.tsx              the one bootstrap: createMfe({ routeTree, widgets, registrations })
src/routes/              TanStack folder routes (prefix-relative); routeTree.gen.ts is generated
src/widgets/             components exposed through createWidget (own React root each)
src/lib/storage.ts       createPlatformStorage stores (namespaced, schema-backed)
src/lib/api.ts           data access: usePlatformFetch (shell token) + the runtime env
src/platform.d.ts        Register augmentation: typed env and feature flags
src/__tests__/           unit tests with renderMfe from @platform/mfe-react/testing
.platform/identity.json  persisted mfeId (commit it; never edit generated files)
```

## Running inside a shell

`pnpm dev` serves this remote; a shell loads it through a manifest override. Point one at
`http://localhost:5173/platform-manifest.json` with `?platform.override.__MFE_ID__=<url>`, the
override control in the shell's developer tools, or the runtime configuration. The dev manifest
carries `dev.hmr = true`, so edits hot-reload inside the shell; production builds never do.

That works against a shell you run locally and against a deployed development shell, which is
how you iterate with real authentication.

See `AGENTS.md` for the canonical patterns and `llm.txt` for the short reference.
